<title>SOUTH AFRICA: PERSKOR LIFTS YR SHR, DIV.</title>
<headline>PERSKOR LIFTS YR SHR, DIV.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended June 30 1996  </p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)	 </p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     1,248.61    vs    607.73</p>
<p>Shr, excluding</p>
<p>    exceptional items	 758.22    vs    607.73</p>
<p>Div (cts)</p>
<p>    - final			84.00    vs     66.00  </p>
<p>    - total		     105.00    vs     84.00   </p>
<p>    Attrib income		 3.64    vs	1.98</p>
<p>    Pre-tax income	    129.93    vs     68.06 </p>
<p>    Tax			    28.09    vs     21.62  </p>
<p>    Turnover		  1,019.16    vs    801.58</p>
<p>Div payable around December 1 </p>
<p>on register October 11</p>
<p>Full name: Perskorgroep Ltd (printing and publishing)</p>
<p>    Share of associates'	0.02    vs	3.35     </p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  39.91    vs	 -    </p>
<p>NOTE - The group said the depreciation in the exchange rate</p>
<p>of the rand, interest rate increases and a levelling out in</p>
<p>consumer spending contributed to a less optimistic view of</p>
<p>trading conditions for the coming year.</p>
<p>However, it remained optimistic that moderate growth in</p>
<p>existing operations could still be achieved. A proposed</p>
<p>reorganisation of the company and of the Perskor group of</p>
<p>companies and the acquisition of Kagiso Publishers Limited, if</p>
<p>approved by shareholders, would further contribute to growth.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
